      "textEn": "137\n\nThus; having said, Bhagavan (God) struck Shalva with his mace, Bhima (Bhagwan) with his mace, and he was terrified.\nWith speed; he struck; on the shoulder; he was enraged; he was furious; he was angry; he was startled; he was trembling; he was in a state of\nfear; he was bloody. Saying this, the angry Lord swung his mace with terrifying power and extreme speed,\nand struck it on the shoulder bone of Shalva, causing him to writhe and vomit blood. Gadayam sannivruttayam shalvastvantharadhiyat. Then, the auspicious time arrived, and the man was lifted up. I am sent by God, thus saying, he wept. 21. Meaning of the word:\n\nGadayam—of the mace; Sannivrittayam—after returning; Shalva—Shalva; Tu—but; Antaradhiyat—became invisible; Tatah—Then; Muhurte—in a moment; Aagatya—coming; Purusha—person; Shirsa—with the head; Achyutam—to Lord Krishna;\nDevakya—by Mother Devaki; Prahitah—entered; Asmi—I; Iti—saying this; Natvya—bowing; Praah—spoke;\nVachah—these words; Rudan—weeping.\nBut as soon as Lord Achyuta took back his mace, Shalva disappeared from sight, and\nA moment later, a person came to God. Bowing before them, he said,\n\"Devaki has sent me,\" and crying, he said the following words. Krishna Krishna, the mighty one, the father, the father-loving one. Having bound himself, like a cow, a dog, and a lion. 22. Meaning of the word.\n\nKrishna Krishna—Hey Krishna, hey Krishna; Maha-baho—Hey mighty-armed ones; Pita—Father; Te—Yours; Pitru—Of your parents; Vatsal—Hey dear; Baddhva—By binding; Tanayah—Taken away; Shalven—By Shalva; Souniken—By butcher;\nYatha—As; Pashu—Domestic animal. [ That person said ]: Hey Krishna, Hey Krishna, Hey mighty-armed one, Hey beloved of your parents, Shalva\nHe has tied up your father and taken him away in the same way that a butcher takes an animal to slaughter.\nFor that reason. [^1]: Nishamya vipriyam krishnam manusim prakritim gatam. Vimansko ghruni snehadvabhashe prakrito yatha. 23 ज़a. Lexicon"
