      "textEn": "139\n\nLiving in. I'll cut ya for your eyes now. You blockhead! If you save it,\nIf you can save it, then save it. And, having abandoned the illusory, the thunderbolt of the demon. Having offered the head, he entered the seat of the seat. 27. Meaning of the word\n\nEvam—in this way; Nirbhartsya—jokingly; Maya-vi—magician; Khadgen—with his sword; Aanakadundubheha—Shri\nVasudeva's; Utkritya—cut; Shirah—head; Aadaya—taking; Kh—in the sky; Sthambh—stable; Saubham—in Saubha;\nSamavishat—entered; Ghruta—entered. In this way, after making God laugh, the magician Shalva appeared to be cutting off Vasudeva's head with his sword. He, taking that head with him, entered the Sauabh Yaan, which was hovering in the sky.\nHe entered. Then the auspicious time is revealed.\nHe knows his own self, and is not attached to his own people.\nThe great one, the knower of the essence, the demon,\nThe illusion, the one who is born of Shalya, the one who is created by me. 28 ”. Meaning of the word\n\nTatah—Then; Muhurta—For a moment; Prakrutau—In normal (human) nature; Upaplutah—Leaning; Swa-bodhaḥ—(though)\nCompletely endowed with self-realization; Aste—Staying; Swa-jana—For one's own loved ones; Anusangatah—Due to affection; Maha-anubhavaḥ—\nThe master of the great power of experience; Tat—That; Abudhyat—Recognized; Asurim—Attached to demons; Mayam—Enchanting\nMagic; Saha—He; Shalva—By Shalva; Prasrutam—Introduced; Maya—By magical illusion; Uditaḥ—Evolved. Lord Krishna is by nature full of knowledge and has the power of immense experience. So,\nwith great affection towards loved ones, for a moment they were absorbed in the posture of an ordinary being.\nThey were absorbed. But they immediately remembered that this is the demonic illusion created by the Maya demon,\nwhich Shalva is bringing into play. Neither there was a messenger nor the body of the father.\nBecame enlightened today, seeing the unpolluted.\nLike a dream, as if a chamber-dweller, an enemy,\nSeeing the beautiful one, he is eager to kill. 29). Lexicon"
